    "title": "Storefront Studio 5b: the four themes as the pages' starting styles",
    "why": "decisions/0159 step 5b (Jason, 2026-11-14: start 5b). A storefront's theme (Canyon, Sage, Paper, Night; 0139) is now the whole look of its pages' blocks: page color, words, heading font, button shape and color, section corners, and the two section backgrounds, named by the theme (Sand and Clay, Sage and Stone, Linen and Honey, Ember and Dusk). Blocks hold no colors of their own, so a change of theme or accent restyles every page at once. The portal's builder shows the page in its theme, as trvgo.us does. Our own pages keep the brand's look (the kit's defaults are unchanged).",
